[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: One export becomes the snapshot and two queryable tables

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[MECHANISM]
UID: MECH-SDOC-BOARD-ADAPTER
TITLE: One export becomes the snapshot and two queryable tables
DEPTH: implemented
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
adapter.py turns one workspace.export index into the sdoc-board/2 snapshot and the sdoc-perspective/2 tables in one pass. The caller supplies the type declarations returned by workspace.grammar, so the adapter neither parses grammar.sgra nor imports StrictDoc. The current branch still supplies a UID-to-file map from the worktree because the daemon export path field lands separately in R2; once that stack is combined, the exported document path replaces this temporary join.

The snapshot keeps one record per node, resolved Parent and Child edges, unresolved-target diagnostics, element-grained File relations, and the caller-supplied sdoc-semantics/2 payload. The Perspective tables retain union-shaped rows so column inference is stable. Extractor lookup for optional File relation KIND values remains an enrichment and may yield null without changing the declared target.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The spike squashed relations into comma-joined facet strings on the node row;
Perspective cannot explode a string back into rows, so relations were
unqueryable (the operator's report, 2026-09-01). The denormalized second table
is the fix.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Updated 2026-09-03 for commits 6fbaa76b, 7d6886d1 and 46cd3cf1: File
relations became element-grained in both payloads, the KIND word is joined
from the extractor, and the snapshot gained the semantics key.

Corrected 2026-09-08: the payload the caller passes in is sdoc-semantics/2,
not /1. The engine's SCHEMA and adapter.py's SEMANTICS_SCHEMA both read
sdoc-semantics/2; the statement had been carrying the older string. The two
schema strings the adapter itself owns, sdoc-board/2 and sdoc-perspective/2,
are unchanged.
<<<
